Optimal Solution - Use a single-pass sliding window to compute the maximum sum of a strictly ascending subarray.
                   “This is a constrained Kadane’s approach where I only extend the window if the sequence remains strictly increasing, otherwise I reset.”

class Solution {
    public int maxAscendingSum(int[] nums) {
        int n = nums.length; // Length of array
        int maxSum = nums[0]; // Stores maximum ascending subarray sum
        int sum = nums[0]; // Current ascending subarray sum
        // Traverse from second element
        for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {
            // If strictly increasing, extend current subarray
            if (nums[i] > nums[i - 1]) {
                sum += nums[i];
            }
            // Otherwise, reset sum to current element
            else {
                maxSum = Math.max(maxSum, sum);
                sum = nums[i];
            }
        }
        // Final comparison after loop
        return Math.max(maxSum, sum);
    }
}

Time Complexity :- O(N).
Space Complexity :- O(1).
